er_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8b461cc37e750e66dc3f06011eac1406ebe5c3b339917e87900f82ab77442bca","event_uuid":"68f7c39b-c37e-4095-a887-93f6c9861501","position":{"commit_sha":"2db8df8aea4c853fb642d410de71a359a8e497b5","position":"1786101585553622001-68f7c39b-c37e-4095-a887-93f6c9861501"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0e8ef729f466bd6a2a7969e5ae6b2c3718614237ee71bff49acf07755fa62e09","event_uuid":"2e01f6ac-5bd6-4a4a-9461-6b53a99101c5","position":{"commit_sha":"2db8df8aea4c853fb642d410de71a359a8e497b5","position":"1786101586682246001-2e01f6ac-5bd6-4a4a-9461-6b53a99101c5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d6b7b688fd38f82979dc5c93195261897b7fa9c7ebaa077be1cf40cbb2607bd9","event_uuid":"b8d46df9-eb44-4e49-bba1-f1bcd50edf6f","position":{"commit_sha":"1e884e61573dfdd3eb6f68a166a28d21135e7f70","position":"1786103401782086001-b8d46df9-eb44-4e49-bba1-f1bcd50edf6f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-224_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"71441096-fe6a-495c-aef3-76e194ce469c","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1493\n\nConfirmed the root cause before editing rather than taking the report on faith. `pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish` uploads a PEP 740 bundle carrying the `https://docs.pypi.org/attestations/publish/v1` predicate to **PyPI's** attestation store; `gh attestation verify --repo` reads **GitHub's** Artifact Attestations store, which holds SLSA provenance. Different stores, different predicates — the documented command could never have worked, and its failure mode reads as \"this release is unattested\" rather than \"you asked the wrong service\", which is the part that makes it a bug rather than a typo.\n\nChanges:\n- `docs/releasing.md`: the consumer recipe is now `pypi-attestations verify pypi --repository https://github.com/navapbc/rebar pypi:nava_rebar-X.Y.Z-py3-none-any.whl` (the official verifier, per pypi/pypi-attestations), plus a callout keeping the two stores distinct and recording the 0.11.0 evidence. GitHub's immutable-release attestation is preserved as the separate guarantee it is.\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`: the `attestations: true` comment now names the PyPI store, the predicate URL, and the correct consumer verifier. No publish-behaviour change.\n- `tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py`: four cells pinning the documented command, the `--repository` identity, the predicate URL, and the workflow comment.\n\nOne design note on the negative assertion: the obvious form (`\"gh attestation verify\" not in doc`) would forbid the prose that explains WHY the GitHub verifier is wrong — the most valuable sentence in the section. So it parses the fenced code blocks and asserts none of them offers that command as a runnable recipe. Prose about the wrong store stays allowed, and wanted.","timestamp":1786103401782086001}],"created_at":1786085650260876001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"433b2c54-97d4-47e7-8902-585e668a10a5","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9874-b1a9-2ff1-4cd3"}],"description":"## Context\nThe rebar 0.11.0 post-release check proved that `gh attestation verify <wheel> --repo navapbc/rebar` cannot verify the PEP 740 bundle produced by pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish. The command queries GitHub Artifact Attestations for SLSA provenance; the publish action uploads a `https://docs.pypi.org/attestations/publish/v1` bundle to PyPI. The official `pypi-attestations verify pypi` command validates the published wheel successfully.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a regression oracle for the documented provenance-verification command/semantics.\n- Replace the incorrect GitHub-store verifier in docs/releasing.md with the authoritative PyPI PEP 740 verifier and correct the matching release-workflow comment.\n- Preserve the separate GitHub immutable-release attestation semantics without conflating them with PyPI provenance.\n- Run focused documentation/workflow tests and the relevant gates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The runbook verifies a downloaded PyPI artifact with the official PyPI attestation verifier and repository identity.\n- [ ] The runbook no longer claims that a GitHub SLSA lookup proves the PyPI PEP 740 bundle.\n- [ ] The release workflow comment names the correct consumer verifier and store.\n- [ ] A regression test protects the documented command and predicate/store distinction.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, and typecheck pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/releasing.md","reason":"replace incorrect GitHub-store verifier with authoritative PyPI PEP 740 verification"},{"path":".github/workflows/release.yml","reason":"correct consumer-verifier comment without changing publish behavior"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py","reason":"regression coverage for documented verifier and store/predicate distinction"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"68f7c39b-c37e-4095-a887-93f6c9861501","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["release","docs","supply-chain"],"ticket_id":"13b4-c597-200b-4e31","ticket_type":"bug","title":"PyPI provenance runbook uses GitHub-only attestation verifier","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4b53f730-ee00-48c0-b657-b8259b0eb6ec","62a13381-6d61-4054-a942-844e663b50be","433b2c54-97d4-47e7-8902-585e668a10a5","68f7c39b-c37e-4095-a887-93f6c9861501","2e01f6ac-5bd6-4a4a-9461-6b53a99101c5","b8d46df9-eb44-4e49-bba1-f1bcd50edf6f"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786103401782086002,"uuid":"f5f91121-f9a0-4de5-af79-75d05798d110"}